        "targets": [
          {
            "id": "sacrifice",
            "selector": { "controller": "self", "zone": "play", "type": "character" },
            "count": 1
          }
        ],
        "effects": [
          { "type": "destroy", "target": { "type": "selected", "id": "sacrifice" } }
        ]
      },
      "abilities": [
        {
          "id": "marauding-madster-recycle",
          "type": "replacement",
          "replaces": { "event": "moveToZone", "zone": "discard", "controlledBy": "self" },
          "condition": {
            "type": "cardNameEquals",
            "target": { "type": "selected", "id": "__candidate" },
            "other": "source"
          },
          "effects": [
            { "type": "moveCard", "target": { "type": "selected", "id": "__candidate" }, "to": "deck" },
            { "type": "shuffleDeck", "player": "controller" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "notes": "Replacement condition uses cardNameEquals(__candidate, source) (the proven Nattering Stoopswaggler / Golemizer idiom) rather than the slice's sourceIsEventCard -- applyReplacement builds no event-bearing context, so sourceIsEventCard would never match. Downside: also matches other in-play copies of this card, but the effect is idempotent. 'from anywhere' is limited to from-play: replacement abilities only run while their source is in play and only replace moves out of play, so a discard directly from hand/deck is not caught."
  },

